Q: Multiple similar scanners with GNU Flex A: <p>Start condition names are just plain integers. You can save and restore them in an <code>int</code> variable. So your &quot;plain identifier&quot; rule would be:</p>
<pre><code>[a-z][a-z]*                  BEGIN(yyextra-&gt;start); return IDENTIFIER;
</code></pre>
<p>and elsewhere to capture the current state you would do:</p>
<pre><code>                             yyextra-&gt;start = YY_START;
</code></pre>
<p>or alternatively, force the state to a known value:</p>
<pre><code>                             yyextra-&gt;start = OLDFORMAT;
                             yyextra-&gt;start = NEWFORMAT;
</code></pre>
